# The live GNOME settings database, not configuration. dconf replaces a symlink with a
# plain file the next time it writes, and gnome-shell keeps the file mapped, so Stow can
# never own it and moving it aside to make room would discard the desktop settings. The
# tracked file is a 2023 snapshot of just two Eye of GNOME settings (a black viewer
# background), committed as "This is a placeholder". Settings travel with `dconf dump`
# and `dconf load` instead (.local/scripts/gnome_path and .local/scripts/cinnamon_path).
^/\.config/dconf(/|$)
